  <section class="tb-hero">
    <span class="eyebrow">The White Plague · <em>Mycobacterium tuberculosis</em></span>
    <h1 class="disp">The <span class="light">world</span><br><span class="gold">consumption created.</span></h1>
    <p class="lede">Before we called it tuberculosis, we called it <em>consumption</em> — and it consumed everything: our cities, our art, our medicine, our dead. It shaped how we build, breathe, and grieve. Two centuries on, it is once again the deadliest infectious disease on Earth — and we have had a cure since 1943.</p>
